# Mana Battle game server — Caddy TLS reverse proxy for the bare deployment.
#
# TEMPLATE: server/scripts/setup-bare.sh substitutes {{MANA_API_DOMAIN}} and
# writes the result to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (Caddy's apt package runs a
# systemd service that reads that file).
#
# Requirements:
#   - a DNS record for the domain pointing at this droplet. DNS-only (grey
#     cloud) is enough — Caddy auto-issues Let's Encrypt certs. If the record
#     is proxied by Cloudflare instead, keep SSL mode at "Full (strict)" so
#     the origin speaks TLS too.
#   - ports 80 (ACME HTTP-01 challenge) and 443 open in the firewall
#     (setup-bare.sh opens them via ufw).
#   - the game server listening on 127.0.0.1:8787 (systemd unit
#     mana-server.service). Caddy forwards X-Forwarded-For and the server
#     sets `trust proxy: loopback`, so auth rate limiting still sees the real
#     client IP.

{{MANA_API_DOMAIN}} {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
}
